---
import Main from "../../layouts/Main.astro";
---

<Main
  title="The District - SyncID Labs"
  description="The HI-Tech Innovation District: a dense, mixed-use district on 89 acres in Markham, with labs, greenhouses, a sovereign-compute test-bed, and a battery-recycling facility."
  lang="en"
  activePath="/district"
>
  <section class="border-b border-neutral-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900">
        The HI-Tech Innovation District
      </h1>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
        <p>
          The HI-Tech Innovation District is a dense, mixed-use, arcology-like district on 89 acres
          in Markham, with on-site innovator residency, labs, greenhouses for food sovereignty, a
          sovereign-compute test-bed, and a battery-recycling facility.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900">The five-year proof</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
        In five years this land will hold working labs, greenhouses, a sovereign-compute test-bed,
        and a battery-recycling facility. Concrete, revenue-generating, and visible.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900">Why a district, not a park</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
        We build the founder pipeline first, then the buildings. A district earns its density from
        the people and ventures inside it, not from the real estate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Main>
